djs for VS Code: the djs compiler (a TypeScript port of the LDC 1.43.0 D compiler frontend) and its VS Code extension

Copyright (c) 2026 Paolo Invernizzi.
Parts derived from the DMD frontend: Copyright (c) 1999-2026 by The D Language Foundation.
Parts derived from LDC's own sources: Copyright (c) 2007-2017 LDC Team.

djs and its extension (host/, extension/, tests/vscode/, language-configuration.json) are distributed under the Boost
Software License, Version 1.0 (full text below), with the exceptions listed under "Derived sets". Each set keeps
the copyright and licence of the code it was ported from.


Derived sets
============

1. The DMD frontend. src/dmd/ is a port of LDC 1.43.0's dmd/ directory, the DMD frontend originally written by Walter
   Bright and maintained by The D Language Foundation, released under the Boost Software License, Version 1.0.

2. LDC's own sources. The files below port, or follow, code from LDC's gen/, driver/ and ir/ directories, cited by
   path and line in each file. That code is distributed under the three-clause BSD LDC license (full text below), and
   so are the parts of these files derived from it:

       src/djs.ts
       src/dmd/argtypes_aarch64.ts     src/dmd/argtypes_sysv_x64.ts    src/dmd/builtin.ts
       src/dmd/cond.ts                 src/dmd/deps.ts                 src/dmd/dmodule.ts
       src/dmd/doc.ts                  src/dmd/dsymbol.ts              src/dmd/dsymbolsem.ts
       src/dmd/expression.ts           src/dmd/globals.ts              src/dmd/iasm/gcc.ts
       src/dmd/init.ts                 src/dmd/inline.ts               src/dmd/inlinecost.ts
       src/dmd/json.ts                 src/dmd/main.ts                 src/dmd/mangle/cpp.ts
       src/dmd/mangle/index.ts         src/dmd/mars.ts                 src/dmd/objc.ts
       src/dmd/pragmasem.ts            src/dmd/root/ctfloat.ts         src/dmd/root/dmdformat.ts
       src/dmd/statementsem.ts         src/dmd/target.ts               src/dmd/templatesem.ts
       src/dmd/typinf.ts
       src/driver/cpreprocessor.ts
       src/gen/dpragma.ts              src/gen/ldctraits.ts            src/gen/llvmhelpers.ts
       src/gen/semantic.ts             src/gen/uda.ts

   LDC's LICENSE notes that driver/ldmd.cpp and gen/typinf.cpp are partly derived from DMD (Boost).

3. LLVM. A few functions in src/driver/cpreprocessor.ts and src/gen/ldctraits.ts model the behaviour of LLVM support
   routines, cited by path in their comments. LLVM is distributed under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions.

4. The import tree. ldc-1.43.0/import is LDC 1.43.0's import directory, unmodified (druntime, Phobos and LDC's own D
   modules), under the licences in ldc-1.43.0/LICENSE, LDC's own: druntime and Phobos under the Boost Software
   License, Version 1.0; ldc/profile.di under the University of Illinois Open Source License and the MIT License.

6. The D grammar. syntaxes/d.tmLanguage.json is code-d's syntaxes/d.json, unmodified, distributed under the MIT
   License: Copyright (c) 2015 Jan Jurzitza (code-d) and Copyright (c) 2014 Jan Van Uytven (the grammar). The full
   notices and the commit it was taken from are in syntaxes/LICENSE-code-d.


Not included: LDC's x86 DMD-style inline assembler parser (gen/asm-x86.h, with gen/asmstmt.cpp), which LDC
incorporates from code written by David Friedman for GDC, released under the Artistic license or the GNU General
Public License. djs's own src/gen/asmstmt.ts keeps a DMD-style `asm` block on x86_64 unanalysed and warns about it.


